<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33201" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Othryădes</span></b> , ae,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀθρυάδης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a male proper name.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The son of Othrys</i>, i. e. <i>Panthus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Panthus Othryades,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 2, 319</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A Spartan general</i>, <i>who</i>,
				<i>in a battle against the Argives</i>, <i>was the sole survivor</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 2,
				665</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Max. 3, 2, 4</span></i>
			<i>ext.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
